# CODEOWNERS — who must approve a pull request, by path.
# With the ruleset's "Require review from Code Owners" rule and 0 required
# approvals, a PR needs approval only if it touches a path that has an owner.
# The last matching pattern wins; a pattern with no owner means no review.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEFAULT — the developer reviews everything else: code, config, workflows,
# dependencies, the CMS setup (public/admin/) and this file itself.
# Deny-by-default, so new paths are protected without being listed here.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* @PanoEvJ

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTENT — no owner, so editors publish directly from the CMS.
# These are the only paths Decap CMS writes to (collection folders, the site
# settings files and media_folder in public/admin/config.yml); the translation
# and image bots write only to src/content/ and public/images/.
# src/data/ holds only the YAML settings files. The build checks them
# (src/lib/site-settings.ts), so a wrong value cannot go live. Keep code out of
# src/data/: it would get no review.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/content/
/src/data/
/public/images/
